Construct the known component $\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\,(0, -5)=(0, -5). \\
\overrightarrow{AC} &=(10, 0).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](assets/3195bc04507885dc01f7b8aad2afc73ac33d535aa434d5120a37774d650be30d.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, 0)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Horizontal scale} &=\frac{10}{4}=\frac{5}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{AC}=\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OA}+\overrightarrow{AC} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{b} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{b}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{5}{2}$.

Construct the known component $\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\,(2, 0)=(2, 0). \\
\overrightarrow{BC} &=(0, -7).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](assets/37672a18f9d2a03e063269730806a2338d4705294bd507630708496cdba27808.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, -2)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Vertical scale} &=\frac{-7}{-2}=\frac{7}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{BC}=\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OB}+\overrightarrow{BC} \\
&=\mathbf{b}+\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{a} \\
&=\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{a}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{7}{2}$.

